hold on, hold on. Let me re-derive cloneBatchedColumnMajor. In ATen:
```cpp
Tensor cloneBatchedColumnMajor(const Tensor& src) {
  auto result = at::empty_strided(src.sizes(), src.transpose(-2,-1).strides(), src.options());
  result.copy_(src);
  return result;
}
```
`src.transpose(-2,-1).strides()` gives the strides of the transposed view, i.e., column-major strides for src's sizes. So the result has shape = src.sizes() and column-major strides. So result(i,j) = src(i,j) in a column-major buffer. The LAPACK call then sees the matrix result = src logically. Then after getrf, LAPACK wrote the LU into the same buffer, and the caller does `lu.copy_(A_.mT())`? Hmm, in `lapackLu`:
